<title>USA: Southern Peru Q1 copper price rose.</title>
<headline>Southern Peru Q1 copper price rose.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Peru Copper Corp reported the following first quarter metal prices, production and sales.</p>
<p>			    Average Metal Prices</p>
<p>							     1997	1996</p>
<p> Copper (per pound - LME)			   $1.10     $1.17</p>
<p> Silver (per ounce - COMEX)			  5.01	5.54</p>
<p>Molybdenum (per pound -</p>
<p>   Metals Week Dealer Oxide)			 4.38	3.97</p>
<p>			  Metal Production and Sales</p>
<p>Copper (000s pounds)</p>
<p>    Mined					     164,500   161,600</p>
<p>    Refined					   149,100   127,400</p>
<p>    Sales					     172,000   169,000</p>
<p>Silver (000s ounces)</p>
<p>    Mined						   619	 651</p>
<p>    Refined						 566	 557</p>
<p>    Sales						   679	 819</p>
<p>Molybdenum (000s pounds)</p>
<p>    Mined						 2,200     1,769</p>
<p>    Sales						 2,234     1,867</p>
<p>Company is 54.1 pct owned by ASARCO Inc and 13.9 percent owned by Phelps Dodge Corp.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859-1610))</p>
